KG42.register("rules-c8d51b4b1ec8bb4c3ca4800a",{"id":"10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R002","paper":"10-hierarchical_coordination","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R002","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Supply submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"Submitted supply-offer curves must be ascending. Scope: First-stage supply-offer submissions in the local P2P energy market. Submitted offers are obtained from the prosumer's independent stochastic bidding optimization, minimizing expected cost minus expected profit subject to constraints (4)-(13), using probabilistic scenarios of electricity price, generation and consumption. Scope: Supply offers produced by the proposed prosumer bidding strategy for each time slot. Condition: When the prosumer submits a supply offer.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.supply under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.supply"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"First-stage supply-offer submissions in the local P2P energy market. | Supply offers produced by the proposed prosumer bidding strategy for each time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-e03","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e14"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-X001","symbol":"P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega}","meaning":"Energy quantity of offering (supply-offer quantity) of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario/block omega, used in the ascending-offering constraint.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy quantity (unit not stated in the source nomenclature); source Eq. (12) constrains its ordering across scenarios/blocks.","unit":null,"indices":["j","t","omega"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-en3"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-X002","symbol":"\\mathcal{O}_{jt}","meaning":"Offer vector for prosumer j at time t, represented as an ordered pair of offering-quantity blocks and offering-price blocks.","kind":"operational","domain":"Ordered pair of lists: a list of offering quantities [O_{jt1}, ..., O_{jtm}] and a list of offering prices [lambda^o_{jt1}, ..., lambda^o_{jtm}] (source Eq. (14)).","unit":null,"indices":["j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-en3"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-X003","symbol":"O_{jtm}","meaning":"Offering quantity of prosumer j in block m and time t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy quantity block (unit not stated in the source nomenclature).","unit":null,"indices":["j","t","m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-en3"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-X004","symbol":"\\lambda^{o}_{jtm}","meaning":"Offering price of prosumer j in block m and time t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Price (currency per energy unit; source does not state the unit in the nomenclature).","unit":null,"indices":["j","t","m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-en3"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-T001","symbol":"\\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega}","meaning":"Predicted energy trading price in the LEM for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario omega; explicitly identified in the source as an input parameter of the prosumer decision-making problem and used to order supply-offer blocks.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"Currency per energy unit (unit not stated in the source nomenclature).","indices":["j","t","omega"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g01-en3","v141-b-g01-e07"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Submitted supply-offer curves must be ascending. Scope: First-stage supply-offer submissions in the local P2P energy market.","expression":"P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} \\ge P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega'}, \\quad \\forall \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} \\ge \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega'}, \\ \\forall \\omega \\ge \\omega', \\ \\forall j, \\ \\forall t","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R002-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R002-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted offers are obtained from the prosumer's independent stochastic bidding optimization, minimizing expected cost minus expected profit subject to constraints (4)-(13), using probabilistic scenarios of electricity price, generation and consumption. Scope: Supply offers produced by the proposed prosumer bidding strategy for each time slot. Condition: When the prosumer submits a supply offer.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-e03","v141-b-g02-e14"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The submitted supply offer of prosumer j at time t is represented as the ordered pair of its offering-quantity blocks [O_{jt1}, ..., O_{jtm}] and the corresponding offering-price blocks [lambda^o_{jt1}, ..., lambda^o_{jtm}]. Scope: Supply offers produced by the proposed prosumer bidding strategy for each time slot.","expression":"\\mathcal{O}_{jt} = \\{[O_{jt1}, \\ldots, O_{jtm}], [\\lambda^{o}_{jt1}, \\ldots, \\lambda^{o}_{jtm}]\\}, \\forall j, \\forall t","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R002-X002","v141-c-R002-X003","v141-c-R002-X004"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-en3"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":"4","section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"proposed P2P energy market is described in the following. en 2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers 𝑃","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"In this paper, each prosumer is defined as a strategic player which is able to find its optimal offers and bids autonomously based on its energy production/consumption and potential flexibility. Here, we propose optimal offering/biding strategy for prosumers through a stochastic programming based on probabilistic scenarios of the electricity price, generation and consumption. Besides, it is noted that this section does not propose a home (building) energy management system. According to our proposed model, each prosumer has their energy generation/consumption profile, and they make their optimal decisions to trade with other prosumers in the LEM based on their bidding strategies."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"proposed P2P energy market is described in the following. en 2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers 𝑃","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In this way, the objective function for prosumer j, OF^{p}_{j}, presents the difference between its expected cost and expected profit as given in Eq. (1): OF^{p}_{j} = EC^{p}_{j} - EP^{p}_{j}, \\forall j   (1) where EC^{p}_{j} and EP^{p}_{j} represent expected cost and profit for prosumer j, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"A.S. Gazafroudi et al. load constraints in which its total energy reduction must be equal to w energ","equation_id":"(12)-(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Finally, prosumers must submit their ascending offering and descending bidding curves for energy tradings to the LMO. Thus, optimal offering and bidding blocks are given by Eqs. (12) and (13) based on [31], respectively: P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} \\geq P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} \\geq \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\omega \\geq \\omega', \\forall j, \\forall t   (12)   P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} \\leq P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} \\geq \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\omega \\geq \\omega', \\forall j, \\forall t   (13) where both \\omega and \\omega' represent scenarios (offering/bidding blocks). In other words, Eqs. (12) and (13) guarantees that optimal offering and bidding curves are ascending and descending, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"P2 where both 𝜔and 𝜔′ represent scenarios (offering/bidding blocks). In bi other words, Eqs. (12) an","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Thus, the decision making problem of prosumer j in the bottom layer of the distribution network is given as: min OF^{p}_{j}  s.t. : (4)-(13)  In this way, prosumer j is able to make optimal decisions based on bidding strategy independently, and submits its offers or bids in each time slot."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":"4","section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"proposed P2P energy market is described in the following. en 2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers 𝑃","equation_id":"(1),(2),(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"OF^{p}_{j} = EC^{p}_{j} - EP^{p}_{j}, \\forall j \\qquad (1)\nEC^{p}_{j} = \\sum_{t\\omega} \\rho_{\\omega}(\\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} + \\lambda^{-}_{t} P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega}), \\forall j \\qquad (2)\nEP^{p}_{j} = \\sum_{t\\omega} \\rho_{\\omega}(\\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} + \\lambda^{+}_{t} P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega}), \\forall j \\qquad (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":"5","section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"A.S. Gazafroudi et al. load constraints in which its total energy reduction must be equal to w energ","equation_id":"(12),(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} \\geq P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} \\geq \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\omega \\geq \\omega', \\forall j, \\forall t \\qquad (12)\nP^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} \\leq P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} \\geq \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\omega \\geq \\omega', \\forall j, \\forall t \\qquad (13)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":"5","section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"P2 where both 𝜔and 𝜔′ represent scenarios (offering/bidding blocks). In bi other words, Eqs. (12) an","equation_id":"(14),(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"O_{jt} = \\{[O_{jt1}, \\ldots, O_{jtm}], [\\lambda^{o}_{jt1}, \\ldots, \\lambda^{o}_{jtm}]\\}, \\forall j, \\forall t \\qquad (14)\nB_{jt} = \\{[B_{jt1}, \\ldots, B_{jtm}], [\\lambda^{b}_{jt1}, \\ldots, \\lambda^{b}_{jtm}]\\}, \\forall j, \\forall t \\qquad (15)\nMoreover, it is noted that each prosumer cannot act as a seller and a buyer in one time slot simultaneously."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-en3","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p02-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":2,"printed_page":"2","section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"𝑡 g g 𝜆−𝑡 ToU buying price from the grid at time slot 𝑡 𝐿𝑗 Maximum energy consumption for pro- sumer","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Parameters in the first stage: \\beta_{jt} Portion of interruptible loads for prosumer j at time slot t which is between 0 and 1; \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} Predicted energy trading price in the LEM for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; \\lambda^{+}_{t} ToU selling price to the grid at time slot t; \\lambda^{-}_{t} ToU buying price from the grid at time slot t; \\bar{L}_{j} Maximum energy consumption for prosumer j; \\bar{P}_{j} Maximum energy generation (PV capacity) for prosumer j; \\rho_{\\omega} Probability of scenario \\omega; L_{jt\\omega} Energy consumption for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P_{jt\\omega} Energy generation for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega. Variables in the first stage: \\lambda^{p2p}_{jit} The price of P2P energy trading between prosumers j and i at time slot t; \\lambda^{b}_{jtm} Bidding price of prosumer j in block m and time t; \\lambda^{o}_{jtm} Offering price of prosumer j in block m and time t; O_{jt} Offer vector for prosumer j at time t; B_{jt} Bid vector for prosumer j at time t; B_{jtm} Bidding quantity of prosumer j in block m and time t; O_{jtm} Offering quantity of prosumer j in block m and time t; EC^{p}_{j} Expected cost for prosumer j; EP^{p}_{j} Expected profit for prosumer j; Lf,i_{jt\\omega} The amount of interruptible load for prosumer j at time t and scenario \\omega; Lf,s_{jt\\omega} The amount of shiftable load for prosumer j at time t and scenario \\omega; OF^{p}_{j} Objective function for prosumer j; P^{p2p,+,bl}_{jitm} The quantity of offering for P2P trading among prosumers j and i at time slot t and block m; P^{p2p,+}_{jit} Energy that prosumer j sells to prosumer i at time slot t; P^{p2p,-,bl}_{jitm} The quantity of bidding for P2P trading among prosumers j and i at time slot t and block m; P^{p2p,-}_{jit} Energy that prosumer j buys from prosumer i at time slot t; P^{+}_{jt\\omega} Total energy sold of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{-}_{jt\\omega} Total energy purchased of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega} Energy sold to the grid at ToU price by prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega} Energy purchased from the grid at ToU price to prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} Energy quantities of offering for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} Energy quantities of bidding for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; u_{jit} A binary variable representing P2P trading status between prosumers j and i at time slot t; v_{jt\\omega} A binary variable for expressing status of buying/selling in the LEM of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"𝑗 𝑗 𝑗, respectively. Moreover, Eqs. (2) and (3) express expected cost and 𝑃𝑗 profit for prosumer 𝑗, ","equation_id":"(2)-(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Moreover, Eqs. (2) and (3) express expected cost and profit for prosumer j, respectively. EC^{p}_{j} = \\sum_{t\\omega} \\rho_{\\omega}(\\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} + \\lambda^{-}_{t} P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega}), \\forall j   (2)   EP^{p}_{j} = \\sum_{t\\omega} \\rho_{\\omega}(\\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} + \\lambda^{+}_{t} P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega}), \\forall j   (3). According to Eq. (2), the expected cost for player j includes two terms. The first term, \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega}, represents the expected cost of energy trading with other prosumers in LEM in scenario \\omega and time t. The expected cost of energy bought from the grid is represented in the second term, \\lambda^{-}_{t} P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega}. Moreover, Eq. (3) consist of two terms. The first term, \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega}, states the expected profit of energy trading in the LEM, and the second term, \\lambda^{+}_{t} P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega}, states the expected profit of energy sold to the grid. Here, \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} is a parameter (input) of the proposed decision making problem for prosumer j representing energy trading price in the LEM."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"P2 where both 𝜔and 𝜔′ represent scenarios (offering/bidding blocks). In bi other words, Eqs. (12) an","equation_id":"(14)-(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Thus, optimal offering and bidding blocks are ordered according to Eqs. (12) and (13) as seen in Eqs. (14) and (15): \\mathcal{O}_{jt} = \\{[O_{jt1}, ..., O_{jtm}], [\\lambda^{o}_{jt1}, ..., \\lambda^{o}_{jtm}]\\}, \\forall j, \\forall t   (14)   \\mathcal{B}_{jt} = \\{[B_{jt1}, ..., B_{jtm}], [\\lambda^{b}_{jt1}, ..., \\lambda^{b}_{jtm}]\\}, \\forall j, \\forall t   (15) where \\mathcal{O}_{jt} and \\mathcal{B}_{jt} represent offer and bid vectors for prosumers j at time t. Besides, O_{jtm} and \\lambda^{o}_{jtm} state offering quantity and price of prosumer j in block m and time t, and B_{jtm} and \\lambda^{b}_{jtm} express bidding quantity and price of prosumer j in block m and time t."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","quote":"Finally, prosumers must submit their ascending offering and descending bidding curves for energy tradings to the LMO."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","quote":"Here, we propose optimal offering/biding strategy for prosumers through a stochastic programming based on probabilistic scenarios of the electricity price, generation and consumption."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e03","quote":"In this way, the objective function for prosumer j, OF^{p}_{j}, presents the difference between its expected cost and expected profit as given in Eq. (1):"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","quote":"Thus, the decision making problem of prosumer j in the bottom layer of the distribution network is given as: min OF^{p}_{j}  s.t. : (4)-(13)  In this way, prosumer j is able to make optimal decisions based on bidding strategy independently, and submits its offers or bids in each time slot."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"9f31572892af8bd7e1c92dd17911d6410e9d989be4c89ac9b10051fb1658bfd1","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The supply-submission rule contains a source-supported mathematical monotonicity constraint (Eq. (12)) and a source-supported offer-vector definition (Eq. (14)), so it is not non-mathematical. However, the frozen graph has V=[\"bidding.supply\"] and E=[], while the core stochastic optimization referenced by C002 (min OF^p_j s.t. (4)-(13)) spans variables and constraint families that are outside this rule's declared graph nodes. Partial support is therefore formalized for C001 and C003, while C002 remains not_formalized pending C.1 graph revision and B source review.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-X001","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P^{lm,+}_{jt omega} is the supply-offer energy quantity whose monotonic ordering is the core of the supply-submission rule; the sole declared node bidding.supply represents the submitted supply-offer artifact."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-X002","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The offer vector O_{jt} is the submitted supply object defined by source Eq. (14); it binds to the sole supply node bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-X003","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"O_{jtm} is the offering-quantity block component of the submitted supply offer represented by bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-X004","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"lambda^o_{jtm} is the offering-price block component of the submitted supply offer represented by bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-T001","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"lambda^{lm}_{jt omega} is the predicted LEM price input used to order supply-offer blocks in Eq. (12); it is attached to bidding.supply because it parameterizes the supply-offer curve."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The ascending-offer constraint qualifies the supply-offer curve output represented by bidding.supply; the frozen rule E is empty, so no edge is available or asserted."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The offer-vector definition defines the submitted supply object represented by bidding.supply; the frozen rule E is empty, so no edge is available or asserted."}],"revision_requests":["C002 remains not_formalized because the frozen rule graph has V=['bidding.supply'] and E=[], while the source optimization min OF^p_j s.t. (4)-(13) spans supply and demand variables and constraint families outside this rule's declared nodes. C.1 is requested to add source-backed nodes/edges for the prosumer objective and the constraint family (4)-(13), or to narrow the rule scope if only supply-offer monotonicity is intended.","The source defines both P^{lm,+}_{jt omega} (Eq. (12)) and O_{jtm}/lambda^o_{jtm} (Eq. (14)) for offering quantities and prices, but the source does not explicitly equate these notations. C.1/scope review is requested to confirm whether they should be unified or kept as distinct scenario/block and block representations.","Index or set objects for j (prosumer), t (time slot), omega/omega' (scenario/offering-bidding block) and m (offer/bid block) are used in the source expressions but are not represented as typed graph objects in this schema. If the downstream formalization requires them, C.1 should add source-backed indexed set definitions.","The source text identifies lambda^{lm}_{jt omega} as an input parameter in evidence v141-b-g02-e04. C.1 should preserve this parameter status and not reclassify it as a decision variable.","All cited B evidence remains UNREVIEWED in this experiment: independent B source audit/re-extraction is required to verify the exact transcription of Eq. (12), the parameter status of lambda^{lm}_{jt omega}, and the definitions of O_{jtm}/lambda^o_{jtm} before downstream scientific acceptance."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
